---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { page, site, stats, actors, categoryIds } from '../lib/site.js';
const c = page('about');
const crumbs = [{ name: 'Home', url: '/' }, { name: 'About', url: '/about.html' }];
---
<Base title={c.title} description={c.metaDescription} path="/about.html" breadcrumbs={crumbs}>
  <div class="wrap prose">
    <header class="page-hero"><h1>{c.h1}</h1><p class="lede">{c.intro}</p></header>
    <h2>What we build</h2>
    <p>{actors.length} public scrapers across {categoryIds.length} areas: real estate, classifieds, vehicles, e-commerce and reviews, ad libraries, social media, video, search engines, travel, business registries and developer tools. Together they have {stats.users.display} Apify users and {stats.runs.display} runs.</p>
    <h2>How the tools work</h2>
    <p>The tools read public pages or public data endpoints of the source site, and most need no login. A few can use your own session cookie for content you already have access to; it stays in your Apify account.</p>
    <p>You run them on <a href={site.brand.storeProfile} rel="noopener">Apify</a>, which hosts the servers, stores your results and bills usage. Prices are per result or per event and are listed on each tool's page here and on the Store.</p>
    <h2>Support</h2>
    <p>Bugs, missing fields and feature requests go to <a href={`mailto:${site.brand.email}`}>{site.brand.email}</a> or the <a href="/contact.html">contact page</a>. You can also open an issue on the tool's Apify Store page.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
